00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.700
Hello and welcome to this video in which
we'll discuss the benefits of having

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.780
effective working relationships, why they are
important and how to create and maintain them.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.760
Relationships are a crucial part of our
personal and professional lives and they can

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.960
greatly impact our success and happiness.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.169
Creating and maintaining effective working
relationships involves building positive

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:28.030
connections with colleagues, clients,
customers, and other stakeholders that can

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:33.400
enhance productivity, foster teamwork and
contribute to the success of an organisation.

00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:39.500
Creating effective working relationships
takes effort and requires active

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.060
participation from all parties involved.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.489
So how can we create effective
working relationships?

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.659
Communication is key to building
effective working relationships.

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:55.360
Be clear and open in your communication,
actively listen to others, and be willing to

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.280
ask questions to clarify any misunderstandings.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.599
Show respect for others by valuing their
opinions, being mindful of their time and

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:07.550
resources, and recognizing their contributions.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:12.649
Respectful behavior can help build trust
and foster positive working relationships.

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:18.579
Encourage collaboration by actively
seeking out opportunities to work together

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.929
and sharing resources and information.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:25.639
A collaborative approach can lead to better
decision-making and improved outcomes.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.460
Practice empathy by putting yourself in others'
shoes and trying to understand their perspective.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.920
This can help build connections and lead to
more effective communication and collaboration.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.439
Take responsibility for your actions and
commitments, and follow through on your promises.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.179
Being accountable can build
trust and establish credibility.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:55.050
Maintaining a positive attitude can help
create a positive work environment, leading

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.610
to increased productivity and better outcomes.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.579
Avoid negativity, be solution-focused,
and celebrate successes.

00:02:04.449 --> 00:02:08.509
Effective working relationships bring
many benefits, including increased

00:02:08.559 --> 00:02:11.350
trust, support, and collaboration.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:17.140
When we have positive relationships with
others, we feel valued, heard, and understood.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:22.059
These relationships can provide us with a sense
of belonging within teams and organisations.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.630
Additionally, strong relationships
can lead to better communication and

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:31.200
problem-solving skills, which can improve
our ability to work together effectively.

00:02:33.059 --> 00:02:37.489
To maintain effective relationships,
it's important to invest time and effort

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.090
into our interactions with others.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:44.370
This means regularly checking in, staying in
touch, and making an effort to understand the

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.220
perspectives of those we are working with.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.940
It's also important to address any
conflicts or misunderstandings in

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.669
a constructive and timely manner.

00:02:55.509 --> 00:02:58.970
When relationships are not maintained
they are at risk of becoming ineffective.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.530
When this happens it can lead
to poor communication, which

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.520
can result in misunderstandings,
missed opportunities, and errors.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.250
Staff morale and motivation will be reduced
and the orgnisation’s culture can be damaged,

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:20.239
negatively effecting overall performance.Decreased
productivity will put further strain on cross team

00:03:20.239 --> 00:03:26.290
relationships and deadlines may start to be missed
and you may see a decrease in quality of work.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.380
Ultimately this will damage
the company’s reputation.

